<script>
  // Pure content: no $state, no events, no lifecycle - and the document
  // proves it. `csr = false` (innovation #25) keeps the client bundle OUT
  // of this document entirely: no runtime, no state script, zero
  // JavaScript for whoever lands here. The route's render function still
  // rides in the bundle, so a client-side navigation from an interactive
  // page paints it instantly and a static deploy's SPA fallback can
  // render it too - only the DOCUMENT is JS-free.
  export const csr = false;

  // $data is server-side: it resolves during the render, on the baked and
  // the on-demand path alike, with no client code involved.
  let bloomed = $data(async () => 'in full bloom');
  // The `@thorn` token is rewritten by the demo plugin (example/rosefn.config.js)
  // before compilation - the source on disk keeps the token.
  let mark = $data(async () => '@thorn');
</script>

<head>
  <title>The Garden - Rosefn</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A pure content page that ships zero JavaScript.">
</head>

<h1>The Garden</h1>
<p>This page is {bloomed()} {mark()} - and it shipped without a single byte of JavaScript.</p>
<p>No bundle, no state script, no hydration: the document is the whole cost, the way a static site would be - with the framework's data, layouts and head blocks still behind it.</p>
<p><a href="/">Back to the gate</a></p>
